          <p>
            The second is that the cheapest rows are the ones that need no fuel at all. A sleeping bag rated well below freezing and a heated throw on a modest battery keep people warm for days, and they carry no combustion risk. The best plans use propane to make one room comfortable for a few hours in the evening and morning, and let bedding do the work overnight, when everyone is asleep and least able to notice a problem.
