          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Emergency heat is a system, not a single product. A battery carbon monoxide alarm, one cold-rated sleeping bag per person and one closed-off room do most of the work, and they cost less than a heater. Add a Mr. Heater Portable Buddy, or a Big Buddy for a larger room, and you can keep that room comfortable for days on cylinders you can store safely outside.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Use stored battery power for blankets, not space heaters, and never bring a generator, grill or outdoor heater inside. If the cold, the outage or medical needs outrun your plan, leave for a warming center. That decision is part of the plan too.
